cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Robust Hyperspectral Image Classification: TEG-XGBoost"
abstract: >
  Research codebase for robust pixel-wise classification of urban hyperspectral
  imagery (Pavia University dataset) using the Texture-Entropy-Gradient (TEG)
  descriptor paired with XGBoost. The project evaluates algorithmic stability
  under severe Salt-and-Pepper (impulse) noise and benchmarks computational
  efficiency against a PyTorch 3D-CNN baseline in few-shot learning scenarios
  (1%–70% training data).
authors:
